{"duration": 0, "showstudentname": true, "showQuestionGroupNames": false, "extensions": ["D:/NumbasGit/numbas/media/user-extensions\\extracted\\4\\drag_and_drop", "D:/NumbasGit/numbas/media/user-extensions\\extracted\\7\\manual_marking"], "question_groups": [{"questions": [{"name": "Human cells", "extensions": ["manual_marking"], "custom_part_types": [], "resources": [["question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq4-stemCells_MUEDRfG.png", "D:\\NumbasGit\\numbas\\media\\question-resources\\hg-cbio1-0euq4-stemCells_MUEDRfG.png"]], "navigation": {"showfrontpage": false, "allowregen": true, "preventleave": false}, "contributors": [{"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/20/", "name": "Stephen Pollock"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/6/", "name": "Sarah Hirstwood"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/17/", "name": "Kenneth Smith"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/15/", "name": "Mandy Tait"}], "rulesets": {}, "tags": ["hg_chbi1_0euq1"], "functions": {}, "variables": {}, "statement": "<p>There are hundreds of cell types in the human body which originate from stem cells in the early embryo.</p>\n<p><img src=\"resources/question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq4-stemCells_MUEDRfG.png\" alt=\"Embryo cell and stem cells\"/></p>", "metadata": {"description": "<p>hg_chbi1_0euq1</p>", "licence": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International"}, "ungrouped_variables": [], "parts": [{"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>What are stem cells?</p>", "marks": 1, "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Cells that are undifferentiated / unspecialised.", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*(undifferentiated|unspecialised).*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"type": "gapfill", "sortAnswers": false, "unitTests": [], "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "gaps": [{"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedWidth": "0px", "fixedHeight": "0px", "displayAnswer": "Choose an answer from: Is it safer than using the drug directly on volunteers? Is it right to use embryos to extract stem cells? Is it right to deprive sufferers of potential treatment? Is it right to use stem cells rather than animals?", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": "", "marks": 1}], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "prompt": "<p>A well known drug company has developed a drug for the treatment of the symptoms of a particular inherited disease. However, before they can proceed to clinical trials using volunteers, the company has decided to do additional tests in the laboratory using stem cells.</p>\n<p>Suggest an ethical consideration which may influence their decision in using stem cells.</p>\n<p>[[0]]</p>\n<p>{manualmarking_builder('b')}{manualmarking_textarea_width('350px')}{manualmarking_textarea_height('4em')}{manualmarking_render()}</p>", "scripts": {}, "marks": 0}, {"type": "gapfill", "sortAnswers": false, "unitTests": [], "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "gaps": [{"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedWidth": "0px", "fixedHeight": "0px", "displayAnswer": "Tissue stem cells are more differentiated than embryonic stem cells.", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": "", "marks": 1}], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "prompt": "<p>What is the difference between embryonic and tissue stem cells?</p>\n<p>[[0]]</p>\n<p>{manualmarking_builder('c')}{manualmarking_textarea_width('350px')}{manualmarking_textarea_height('4em')}{manualmarking_render()}</p>", "scripts": {}, "marks": 0}, {"type": "gapfill", "sortAnswers": false, "unitTests": [], "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "gaps": [{"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "exact", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedWidth": "0px", "fixedHeight": "0px", "displayAnswer": "regulatory", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": "regulatory", "marks": 1}, {"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "exact", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedWidth": "0px", "fixedHeight": "0px", "displayAnswer": "tumour", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": "tumour", "marks": 1}], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "prompt": "<p>Complete the following sentences.<br/><br/>Cancer cells divide excessively because they do not respond to [[0]] signals. This results in a mass of abnormal cells called a [[1]]. </p>", "scripts": {}, "marks": 0}], "variablesTest": {"maxRuns": 100, "condition": ""}, "preamble": {"js": "", "css": ""}, "variable_groups": [], "advice": "<p>Part b) Choose an answer from:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Is it safer than using the drug directly on volunteers?</li>\n<li>Is it right to use embryos to extract stem cells?</li>\n<li>Is it right to deprive sufferers of potential treatment?</li>\n<li>Is it right to use stem cells rather than animals?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Part c)&nbsp;Tissue stem cells are more differentiated than embryonic stem cells.</p>"}, {"name": "Structure of DNA", "extensions": [], "custom_part_types": [], "resources": [["question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq1-bonds_ahV0emT.png", "D:\\NumbasGit\\numbas\\media\\question-resources\\hg-cbio1-0euq1-bonds_ahV0emT.png"], ["question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq1-DNAnucleotide_xZukups.png", "D:\\NumbasGit\\numbas\\media\\question-resources\\hg-cbio1-0euq1-DNAnucleotide_xZukups.png"]], "navigation": {"showfrontpage": false, "allowregen": true, "preventleave": false}, "contributors": [{"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/20/", "name": "Stephen Pollock"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/6/", "name": "Sarah Hirstwood"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/15/", "name": "Mandy Tait"}], "rulesets": {}, "tags": ["hg_chbi1_0euq2"], "functions": {}, "variables": {}, "statement": "", "metadata": {"description": "<p>hg_chbi1_0euq2</p>", "licence": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International"}, "ungrouped_variables": [], "parts": [{"matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>The following diagram represents the four different nucleotides found in DNA.</p>\n<p><img src=\"resources/question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq1-bonds_ahV0emT.png\" alt=\"Four nucleotides with bonds forming between G and C, and T and A\"/></p>\n<p>Name the type of bond which links the base on one DNA strand to the base on the opposite strand.</p>", "marks": 1, "type": "patternmatch", "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Hydrogen bond", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*hydrogen.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>A section of a DNA molecule contains 8000 bases. Of these, 2800 are thymine. What is the percentage of cytosine bases in the molecule?</p>", "marks": 1, "type": "patternmatch", "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "15%", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": "(15|fifteen).?(%|percent)?", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>What is the name of the sugar present in DNA?</p>", "marks": 1, "type": "patternmatch", "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Deoxyribose sugar", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*deoxyribose.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>The following diagram shows a DNA nucleotide.</p>\n<p><img src=\"resources/question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq1-DNAnucleotide_xZukups.png\" alt=\"DNA nucleotide with labels X (oval), Y (pentagon) and Z (rectangle with right hand edge curved in)\"/></p>\n<p>Identify the part labelled X in the diagram.</p>", "marks": 1, "type": "patternmatch", "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Phosphate", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*phosphate.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Identify the part labelled Y in the diagram.</p>", "marks": 1, "type": "patternmatch", "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Deoxyribose sugar", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*deoxyribose sugar.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Identify the part labelled Z in the diagram.</p>", "marks": 1, "type": "patternmatch", "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Base", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*base.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}], "variablesTest": {"maxRuns": 100, "condition": ""}, "preamble": {"js": "", "css": ""}, "variable_groups": [], "advice": ""}, {"name": "Replication of DNA", "extensions": [], "custom_part_types": [], "resources": [["question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq2-DNAreplication_LM4Yq0x.png", "D:\\NumbasGit\\numbas\\media\\question-resources\\hg-cbio1-0euq2-DNAreplication_LM4Yq0x.png"]], "navigation": {"showfrontpage": false, "allowregen": true, "preventleave": false}, "contributors": [{"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/20/", "name": "Stephen Pollock"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/6/", "name": "Sarah Hirstwood"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/3/", "name": "Daniel Pacey"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/15/", "name": "Mandy Tait"}], "rulesets": {}, "tags": ["hg_chbi1_0euq3"], "functions": {}, "variables": {}, "statement": "<p>This diagram represents DNA replication.</p>\n<p><img src=\"resources/question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq2-DNAreplication_LM4Yq0x.png\" alt=\"DNA replication with label A on a short strand of nucleotides that allow polymerase to add DNA nucleotides and label B on an enzyme that synthesises DNA strands from individual nucleotides\"/></p>", "metadata": {"description": "<p>hg_chbi1_0euq3</p>", "licence": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International"}, "ungrouped_variables": [], "parts": [{"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Name structure A.</p>", "marks": 1, "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Primer", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*primer.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Name one essential requirement for DNA replication that is not shown in the diagram.</p>", "marks": 1, "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Nucleotides / ATP", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*(nucleotides|ATP).*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Name enzyme B.</p>", "marks": 1, "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "DNA polymerase", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*DNA polymerase.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"type": "gapfill", "sortAnswers": false, "unitTests": [], "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "gaps": [{"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "exact", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedWidth": "0px", "fixedHeight": "0px", "displayAnswer": "hydrogen", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": "hydrogen", "marks": 1}, {"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "exact", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedWidth": "0px", "fixedHeight": "0px", "displayAnswer": "heating", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": "heating", "marks": 1}], "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "prompt": "<p>The polymerase chain (PCR) can be used to obtain many copies of a particular gene.</p>\n<p>The [[0]] bonds of DNA are separated by [[1]] during PCR.</p>", "scripts": {}, "marks": 0}, {"prompt": "<p>Primers are required for the process of PCR. Which of the following statements is false?</p>", "variableReplacements": [], "minMarks": 0, "type": "1_n_2", "shuffleChoices": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "distractors": ["", "", "", ""], "displayType": "radiogroup", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "displayColumns": "1", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "matrix": [0, 0, "1", 0], "choices": ["Primers mark the start and end of sequence to be copied.", "Primers prevents the strands re-joining.", "Primers unwind double helix.", "Primers allow DNA polymerase to attach."], "maxMarks": 0, "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "marks": 0}, {"prompt": "<p>Starting with a single molecule of DNA, the polymerase chain reaction goes through three complete cycles. How many molecules of DNA would be produced?</p>", "variableReplacements": [], "minMarks": 0, "type": "1_n_2", "shuffleChoices": false, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "distractors": ["", "", "", ""], "displayType": "radiogroup", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "displayColumns": "1", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "matrix": [0, "1", 0, 0], "choices": ["4", "8", "16", "32"], "maxMarks": 0, "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "marks": 0}], "variablesTest": {"maxRuns": 100, "condition": ""}, "preamble": {"js": "", "css": ""}, "variable_groups": [], "advice": ""}, {"name": "Gene expression", "extensions": ["manual_marking"], "custom_part_types": [], "resources": [["question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq3-proteinSynthesis_S3EmRIR.png", "D:\\NumbasGit\\numbas\\media\\question-resources\\hg-cbio1-0euq3-proteinSynthesis_S3EmRIR.png"]], "navigation": {"showfrontpage": false, "allowregen": true, "preventleave": false}, "contributors": [{"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/20/", "name": "Stephen Pollock"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/6/", "name": "Sarah Hirstwood"}, {"profile_url": "https://assess12test.scholar.hw.ac.uk/accounts/profile/15/", "name": "Mandy Tait"}], "rulesets": {}, "tags": ["hg_chbi1_0euq4"], "functions": {}, "variables": {}, "statement": "<p>This diagram shows the stages of protein synthesis.</p>\n<p><img src=\"resources/question-resources/hg-cbio1-0euq3-proteinSynthesis_S3EmRIR.png\" alt=\"Protein synthesis. Stage X: process where DNA in chromosome is used to produce primary mRNA. Stage Y: where where primary mRNA becomes final mRNA. Stage Z: process where final mRNA is used to form protein\"/></p>", "metadata": {"description": "<p>hg_chbi1_0euq4</p>", "licence": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International"}, "ungrouped_variables": [], "parts": [{"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Name stage X.</p>", "marks": 1, "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Transcription", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*transcription.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Name the exact location in the cell where stage X occurs.</p>", "marks": 1, "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Nucleus", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*nucleus.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Name stage Z.</p>", "marks": 1, "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Translation", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*translation.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Name the exact location in the cell where stage Z occurs.</p>", "marks": 1, "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "Ribosome", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*ribosome.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "prompt": "<p>Which enzyme catalyses stage X of this process?</p>", "marks": 1, "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedHeight": "0px", "variableReplacementStrategy": "originalfirst", "customMarkingAlgorithm": "", "extendBaseMarkingAlgorithm": true, "variableReplacements": [], "displayAnswer": "RNA polymerase", "unitTests": [], "scripts": {}, "answer": ".*RNA polymerase.*", "fixedWidth": "0px"}, {"type": "gapfill", "sortAnswers": false, "unitTests": [], "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "gaps": [{"type": "patternmatch", "matchMode": "regex", "showFeedbackIcon": true, "showCorrectAnswer": true, "fixedWidth": "0px", "fixedHeight": "0px", "displayAnswer": "Choose an answer from: the introns / non-